NAME
    sed - perform stream text substitution

SYNOPSIS
    sed s/pattern/replacement/[gi] [text...]

DESCRIPTION
    Substitutes matches of <pattern> with <replacement> on each line of
    piped standard input, or on trailing literal [text...] when no
    standard input is piped. Only the s/// substitution command is
    supported.

    Any character may serve as the delimiter (for example
    's#/old#/new#'); prefixing the delimiter with '\' matches it
    literally inside the pattern or replacement.

    Patterns use Rust's regex engine (non-quantifier '{' and '}' are
    treated as literals; look-around assertions and back-references are
    not supported). In replacements, '&' expands to the full match and
    '\1' through '\9' expand to capture groups (a group index not
    present in the pattern expands to literal '$N').

OPTIONS
    g   Replace every match on each line (without g, only the first
        match per line is replaced).
    i   Match <pattern> case-insensitively.

EXAMPLES
    regs | sed s/PC=/pc=/
    echo hello world | sed s/o/0/g
    echo foo/bar | sed 's#/#-#g'

EXIT STATUS
    0   Substitution completed (or usage printed with no expression).
    1   Missing input, unsupported command, malformed expression, or
        invalid regular expression.

SEE ALSO
    grep(1), awk(1), echo(1)
